Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): checkpoint recovery no longer deadlocks on its
 own flock [daveey]

The fork runs recover_from_checkpoint under the processes.json flock; upstream's _track_started
(used to adopt a worker's output-log session) writes the checkpoint, which opened a second
descriptor and waited on this thread's own lock forever. Every adopted background process hung
the adopting worker. The lock is now reentrant per thread. Caught by upstream's
test_managed_worker_background_output (red before, green after).
